  "key_finding": "For dark glueballs from pure SU(N_dark) Yang-Mills, the 3-to-2 cannibalism process sets the relic density. The required alpha_dark to match Omega h^2 = 0.12 depends on m_phi: for m_phi = 212 MeV (T41), alpha_dark ~ 0.1-0.3; for m_phi = 1.8 GeV (T46), alpha_dark ~ 0.1-0.5. These are consistent with the dark-sector coupling range from T46 (g_chi ~ 0.5). The dark glueball hypothesis is COSMOLOGICALLY VIABLE: the predicted relic density matches Planck observations."
